Negative control for the bar being APP CHROME (T2.5 · G9 · AC1.1).

Scope is global, so the cluster belongs to the layout header — the one place it
is on screen whatever page is mounted. This mutant leaves the bar fully built,
fully imported and fully rendered; it only moves it out of the header and into
the main content column beside the page. Every assertion that merely finds a
`scope-bar` in the rendered layout stays green, which is exactly the failure
worth pinning: a bar that renders but is no longer chrome is a page element, and
a page element is the thing `G9` deletes.

Re-anchored by T3.2, which owns `default.vue` this wave and retired the header's
own Inspector toggle with it. The mutation is unchanged.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the T2.5 layout case that resolves the bar INSIDE the header's actions
slot, not merely somewhere in the layout.

